# --- Kiosk: Qt5 WebEngine on /dev/fb0 ---
#
# After many attempts to run Cog/WPE on top of VC4 KMS DRM, we hit a
# wall: the rpi3's DSI subdevice in vc4 doesn't bind under our firmware/
# kernel/overlay combo. The DSI connector simply doesn't enumerate as a
# DRM connector — only HDMI does — so Cog has no panel to render to.
#
# Pivot: drop the modern KMS+Wayland+WPE stack and use the legacy
# firmware-driven fbdev path (start.elf drives the DSI panel directly,
# /dev/fb0 is the display). Render with Qt5 WebEngine + the linuxfb QPA
# platform plugin. This is the same architecture the archived
# nerves-web-kiosk/kiosk_system_rpi3 used in 2020.
#
# Qt5 WebEngine is Chromium-based, so HTML5 + JS + WebSocket + LiveView
# all work fine. Compile is slow (~3 hours on this build host) but only
# happens once per system release.
#
# qt5webengine has a hard dependency on libudev (BR2_PACKAGE_HAS_UDEV).
# eudev provides it; restoring eudev requires switching the rootfs
# device-creation method from devtmpfs to eudev so eudev owns /dev.
# BR2_ROOTFS_DEVICE_CREATION_DYNAMIC_DEVTMPFS is not set
BR2_ROOTFS_DEVICE_CREATION_DYNAMIC_EUDEV=y
BR2_PACKAGE_EUDEV=y

BR2_PACKAGE_QT5=y
